f077e91f649a4b955fbf9f71658b9237223f1170.body:
Fix real constants \(C_{\theta},C_g,C_q,\psi_{\eta},\psi_{\xi}\) and \(R_1\). There is a constant \(K>0\) such that, for every sample size \(n\), every parameter tuple whose corresponding constants are \(C_{\theta},C_g,C_q,\psi_{\eta},\psi_{\xi}\) and whose outer radius is \(R_1=R_0+1\), every observed-data law \(P\), and every deterministic split fold \(I_a\) with \(a\in\{0,1\}\), if
\begin{itemize}
\item \textbf{(Sample size.)} \(n\ge 2\);
\item \textbf{(Model class.)} \(P\in\mathcal P_{\mathrm{NG},n}\), as in \(\cref{obj:def:non-gaussian-class}\);
\item \textbf{(Sampling.)} \(O_1,\ldots,O_n\) are i.i.d. from \(P\), as in \(\cref{obj:ass:iid-sampling}\);
\item \textbf{(Fold nonemptiness.)} \(|I_a|\ge 1\);
\end{itemize}
then
\[
\mathbb E_{P^n}\!\left[\sup_{|z|\le R_1}\left|\widehat F_{a,n}(z)-F_n(z)\right|^2\right]
+
\mathbb E_{P^n}\!\left[\sup_{|z|\le R_1}\left|\widehat G_{a,n}(z)-G_n(z)\right|^2\right]
\le
\frac{K}{|I_a|}.
\]

48894a60e25381e46c3a9d1053c11205c9fc7297.body:
Define the non-Gaussian minimax mean-squared risk by
\[
\mathfrak R_n^{\mathrm{NG}}
=
\inf_{\widetilde\theta(O_1,\ldots,O_n;\bar g_n,\bar q_n)}
\sup_{P\in\mathcal P_{\mathrm{NG},n}}
E_P\!\left[(\widetilde\theta-\theta_0(P))^2\right].
\]
Define the Gaussian JMS minimax mean-squared risk by
\[
\mathfrak R_n^{\mathrm G}
=
\inf_{\widetilde\theta(O_1,\ldots,O_n;\bar g_n,\bar q_n)}
\sup_{P\in\mathcal P_{\mathrm G,n}^{\mathrm{JMS}}}
E_P\!\left[(\widetilde\theta-\theta_0(P))^2\right].
\]
For \(0<\gamma<1\), define the Gaussian JMS minimax generalized-quantile risk by
\[
\mathfrak M_{n,1-\gamma}^{\mathrm G}
=
\inf_{\widetilde\theta}
\sup_{P\in\mathcal P_{\mathrm G,n}^{\mathrm{JMS}}}
Q_{P,1-\gamma}\!\left(|\widetilde\theta-\theta_0(P)|\right).
\]

0e5d3c8b3b9ee2a21ea00a01e342fa46b06badf4.body:
The clipped sine-ratio estimator is
\[
\widehat\theta_{\sin,n}
=
\Pi_{[-C_{\theta},C_{\theta}]}
\left\{
\frac{\mathbb P_n[Y\sin(\pi Z_n/2)]}
{\mathbb P_n[Z_n\sin(\pi Z_n/2)]}
\right\},
\]
with fallback value \(0\) when the empirical denominator is below one half of its population lower bound.

fbf583ccf363bf01c8c66b1ef21a09df8754ff1b.body:
For each library depth \(m\), let \(\mathscr C_m\) be a finite deterministic library of rational circles, increasing with \(m\). On prespecified independent folds, form the empirical transforms \(\widehat F_{a,n}\), \(\widehat G_{a,n}\), and their derivatives. For a circle \(C=\{\rho e^{it}:0\le t\le2\pi\}\) on which the empirical denominator is certified positive, the candidate record is restricted to quantities definitionally computed from the empirical contour integrands
\[
 W_{a,C}(t)=\rho e^{it}
 \frac{\widehat F'_{a,n}(\rho e^{it})}
      {\widehat F_{a,n}(\rho e^{it})},
 \qquad
 V_{a,C}(t)=\rho e^{it}
 \frac{\widehat G_{a,n}(\rho e^{it})}
      {\widehat F_{a,n}(\rho e^{it})}.
\]
Specifically, the record may contain the boundary modulus \(\inf_{z\in C}|\widehat F_{a,n}(z)|\), the winding enclosure for \((2\pi)^{-1}\int_0^{2\pi}W_{a,C}(t)\,dt\), the contour-moment enclosure for \((2\pi)^{-1}\int_0^{2\pi}V_{a,C}(t)\,dt\), and the angular variance
\[
 \widehat v_{a,C}
 =\frac1{2\pi}\int_0^{2\pi}
 \left|V_{a,C}(t)-
 \frac1{2\pi}\int_0^{2\pi}V_{a,C}(u)\,du\right|^2dt.
\]
These records are candidate data. The symbol \(\widehat\theta_{\mathrm{ad}}\) is reserved for a future estimator that selects among ordinary DML, finite-order ACE, and contour moments; specifies any contribution formula beyond the displayed empirical integrands; supplies an argmin or tie-breaking prescription; and establishes risk, coverage, critical-scaling, or lower-bound guarantees.

fbd3f5e67fc161924f9bd185c92b8dc734728b93.body:
For every \(n\), compute \(a_{1,n},b_{1,n},a_2,b_{2,n}\) exactly as in condition (21). On indices for which the following expressions are defined, the JMS order-\(r\) eligibility condition \(\mathsf E_n^{\mathrm{JMS}}\) is
\[
r\le
\min\left\{
\frac{b_{1,n}}{a_{1,n}}
-a_{1,n}^{-1}\log\!\left(\frac{b_{1,n}}{a_{1,n}}\right),
\frac{b_{2,n}}{a_2\log(a_2b_{2,n})}
\right\}.
\]

0e1bd12a051da8925f9135288a7760a6d99755ff.body:
Fix any parameter tuple with:
\begin{itemize}
\item \textbf{(Sample size and orders.)} a sample size \(n\ge 1\), integers \(r,k\in\mathbb N\) with \(k=r+1\) and \(r\ge 2\);
\item \textbf{(Exponent and level.)} an exponent \(s\ge r\) and a probability level \(\gamma\in(1/2,1)\);
\item \textbf{(Positive constants.)} constants \(C_{\theta},C_g,C_q,\psi_{\eta},\psi_{\xi},\delta,\sigma>0\);
\item \textbf{(Radius sequences.)} nonnegative nonincreasing sequences \(\varepsilon_1,\varepsilon_2:\mathbb N\to\mathbb R\) on positive indices, with sample-size values \(\varepsilon_{1,n}\) and \(\varepsilon_{2,n}\).
\end{itemize}
On any measurable covariate space, the following hold.
\begin{itemize}
\item \textbf{(Degenerate target.)} For every \(P\in\mathcal P_{\mathrm G,n}^{\mathrm{JMS}}\) satisfying \(\cref{obj:def:gaussian-class}\), the partially linear coefficient obeys
\[
\theta_0(P)=0.
\]
\item \textbf{(Zero minimax risks.)} For any supplied code sequences \(\widehat g,\widehat q:\mathbb N\to\mathcal X\to\mathbb R\), if \(\mathcal P_{\mathrm G,n}^{\mathrm{JMS}}\) contains a law whose clipped treatment and outcome codes agree pointwise at index \(n\) with
\[
x\mapsto \min\{\max\{\widehat g_n(x),-C_g\},C_g\}
\quad\text{and}\quad
x\mapsto \min\{\max\{\widehat q_n(x),-C_q\},C_q\},
\]
then
\[
\mathfrak R_n^{\mathrm G}(p;\widehat g,\widehat q)=0
\quad\text{and}\quad
\mathfrak M_{n,1-\gamma}^{\mathrm G}(p;\widehat g,\widehat q)=0.
\]
\end{itemize}

20e666dc4c2419cb035a1fb37ac2e7d6e292ee69.body:
Given the quantities \(a_{1,n},b_{1,n},a_2,b_{2,n}\) in \(\cref{obj:def:jms-eligibility-quantities}\), define \(\mathsf E_n^{\mathrm{JMS}}\) to be the condition, on indices for which the displayed expressions are defined,
\[
r\le
\min\left\{
\frac{b_{1,n}}{a_{1,n}}
-a_{1,n}^{-1}\log\!\left(\frac{b_{1,n}}{a_{1,n}}\right),
\frac{b_{2,n}}{a_2\log(a_2b_{2,n})}
\right\}.
\]
